From aaf150986f5e2cac9db7be2d75768f8a21942471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] a2dp-sink: register AAC and LDAC sink endpoints (control
 plane)

The Nougat A2DP sink registers a single SBC SNK SEP.  Phones default to
their best codec, so with only SBC advertised they fall back to SBC even
when they could send AAC or LDAC.  This adds the full control plane for
a multi-codec sink:

* stack/a2dp: new a2d_aac.c / a2d_ldac.c with A2D_Bld*/A2D_Pars* for the
  MPEG-2/4 AAC CIE (A2DP spec 4.3.2) and the Sony LDAC vendor CIE
  (vendor id 0x012D, codec id 0x00AA), mirroring a2d_sbc.c.  a2d_api.h
  gains A2D_MEDIA_CT_VEND (0xFF), absent from the r36 tree.
* SEP registration (bta_av_main.c): the SNK role now registers SEPs
  idx 1..BTA_AV_MAX_SEPS-1 by calling the cos.init callout until it
  declines, instead of a single hardcoded index 1.  SRC role unchanged
  (single SEP at idx 0).  With BTA_AV_MAX_SEPS=4 (bdroid_buildcfg.h)
  and AVDT_NUM_SEPS=8/AVDT_CODEC_SIZE=16 (bt_target.h overrides) the
  set is SRC/SBC + SNK/SBC + SNK/AAC + SNK/LDAC.
* bta_av_co.c: AAC and LDAC sink capability tables; init callout cases;
  sink_supports_config accepts M24 and LDAC-VEND configs (cfg_in_cap
  helpers); INT-side codec selection prefers LDAC > AAC > SBC
  (peer_src_supports_codec priority scan + per-codec preferred-config
  builders); setconfig on a SNK SEP now accepts any codec we advertise
  instead of forcing SBC reconfiguration.
* btif_av_api.h/btif_av_co.h: BTIF_AV_CODEC_AAC/LDAC ids and the two new
  SEP indices.
---
